    "reasons": [
      "the cited Langley report (TM-81927) has a text layer with no table of Cp at x/c=0.25 across Mach; its pressure distributions are figures, and the only table is the airfoil section coordinates",
      "the table states neither angle of attack nor Reynolds number, and Cp(0.25) moves by a factor of 2.8 between alpha~0 and alpha=10 in the same source",
      "against the alpha~0 measurement scaled by Prandtl-Glauert, every value from M=0.50 to M=0.80 is a constant 1.475x too negative, which is the signature of a constructed series rather than a measured one"
    ]
